From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Giuseppe Maggio <jertlok@proton.me>
Date: Sat, 8 Aug 2026 18:16:34 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] media: qcom: camss: allocate the ISPIF whenever the SoC
 declares one

The ISPIF is allocated from a hardcoded list of CAMSS versions, which has
fallen out of step with the resource tables: sdm660 ships a full
ispif_res_660, its DT binding requires the ispif register range and
interrupt, and every ISPIF code path already handles CAMSS_660 - but the
version is missing from the list, so camss->ispif stays NULL and
msm_ispif_subdev_init() returns early. The block is described, clocked by
DT and never programmed.

Gate the allocation on the resource table instead. A SoC that describes an
ISPIF gets one, and the list cannot drift again.

Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Giuseppe Maggio <jertlok@proton.me>
---
 drivers/media/platform/qcom/camss/camss.c | 4 +---
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/media/platform/qcom/camss/camss.c b/drivers/media/platform/qcom/camss/camss.c
index 2fbcd0e343aa..c150f1984b50 100644
--- a/drivers/media/platform/qcom/camss/camss.c
+++ b/drivers/media/platform/qcom/camss/camss.c
@@ -4170,9 +4170,7 @@ static int camss_probe(struct platform_device *pdev)
 	if (!camss->csid)
 		return -ENOMEM;
 
-	if (camss->res->version == CAMSS_8x16 ||
-	    camss->res->version == CAMSS_8x53 ||
-	    camss->res->version == CAMSS_8x96) {
+	if (camss->res->ispif_res) {
 		camss->ispif = devm_kcalloc(dev, 1, sizeof(*camss->ispif), GFP_KERNEL);
 		if (!camss->ispif)
 			return -ENOMEM;
